OPEN DESIGN PROBE (not a pass/fail claim): can an owned obligation be carried
across a loop back-edge via consume-in/issue-out? Currently rejected by KORU030.
Already drove the KORU030 "input:owned" hint fix (now user-facing "<owned!>").

================================================================================
DESIGN RESOLVED (2026-06-21, Lars + Claude). REAL gap, and a STATIC checker
extension — NOT a semantic change, NOT a "dynamic" or runtime obligation.
Obligations are compile-time phantoms, ERASED at emit (see 400_106 stripping
`<!active>` from generated Zig). Nothing here is counted at runtime. If an
implementation reaches for a runtime counter / refcount / drain-assert, it has
misread the probe — back out and keep it static.

THE SHAPE (why it's actually sound):
  Exactly ONE obligation is in flight across the @loop back-edge at all times.
  `step` consumes `<!owned>` in and issues `<owned!>` out (`| again` / `| stop`),
  and the #loop/@loop fold feeds that issued handle into the NEXT iteration's
  consuming param. So the loop invariant is: "outstanding owned obligations at the
  back-edge = 1", discharged at the exit (`done` consumes the final `<!owned>`).
  Count is invariantly 1 — a linear loop invariant, NOT a data-dependent count.
  This is statically provable.

WHY IT'S RED:
  The phantom checker does not FOLLOW the obligation through the `@loop`
  re-invocation. It sees `| again *Handle<owned!>` issue an obligation, finds no
  discharge on that syntactic path, and fires KORU030 ("was not discharged") —
  unaware the back-edge hands it to the next iteration's consume.

IMPLEMENTATION TARGET:
  src/phantom_semantic_checker.zig (the KORU030 site; cleanup_obligations
  tracking, ~line 712). Teach it loop-carried linearity: an obligation issued on a
  branch that re-enters a #loop label is satisfied if the loop's consuming
  parameter consumes it on the next pass and the exit branch discharges the final
  one. Recognize the static back-edge invariant; emit nothing extra.

  Sibling probe with the same root: 330_082 (for-loop BODY form, KORU032).
================================================================================
